# Use case: large files where you only need the public interface.
# -l aggressive strips all bodies; use sparingly — Read tool is better for normal reads.
rtk read -l aggressive <file>
```
```

**Remove from the "MUST Prefix" table:** the `rtk read <file>` row (if it exists) — the table currently shows `find`, `grep`, `git`, `npm run`, `tsc`, `docker ps`, `curl`. Verify on line 22-32: the current table does not have a `rtk read` row, so no change needed there.

**Update the "Hook Status" section at the bottom:**

```markdown
## Hook Status (this machine)

```
[ok] PreToolUse hook: installed — auto-rewrites every Bash call via rtk-prerewrite.js
[ok] Manual prefix: still valid as fallback when RTK_DISABLED=1 is needed
